      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (54%):</strong> Residual after de-escalation and escalation scenarios are subtracted; characterized by sustained Hormuz traffic at 5–15% of baseline under the 60-day ceasefire clock, IAEA access unresolved, and HLC meetings intermittent but not collapsed — a contested ceasefire with multiple unresolved core issues, not a diplomatic momentum.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (26%):</strong> P(F10=YES) = 0.22 as primary driver (comprehensive deal by August 17), plus marginal credit of approximately 4% from partial scenarios in which F9 (HLC) succeeds and F11 (Hormuz &#x2265;30 transits) resolves YES without a formal final deal.</p>
